hen node_count is incremented.\n6. Control flow: loop bounds (`<` vs `<=`), break/return placement, recursion order, which branch is taken for each input class.\n7. Any place the Rust caches a global in a local variable where the C re-reads it (or vice versa) — argue whether that can ever be observable.\n\nReport your findings as a list. For each item state: function, the exact C line(s), the exact Rust line(s), whether it is EQUIVALENT or a DIVERGENCE, and for divergences give a concrete input that distinguishes them.\n\nBe skeptical and concrete. Do NOT just say \"looks correct\" — show your reasoning per function. Do NOT modify any files; this is read-only analysis. Report the list of findings as your final answer."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":776,"cache_read_input_tokens":147762,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":776,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e1c21d0a-4bcf-4f52-9a28-e367512a5538","uuid":"25e148cb-8d23-4c6c-882e-144013fc941b","timestamp":"2026-08-19T21:22:11.606Z"}
