{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_5yit7btsawvbzkxkkhp53m6bsnvtmhnchxkeor76wwaaxr63suiq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src/src/lib.c` is a single translation unit exporting **13 symbols** (11 functions + 2 mutable globals `node_table`/`node_count`). Only `inreftree` is in the public header, but the other 10 have external linkage, so all are part of the ABI and all are tested directly through `dlsym`.\n\n## Phase A — surface mapping\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — `nm -D` diff is **empty in both directions**: 13/13 symbols, matching kinds, matching data sizes (`node_table` = 0xa28 = 2600, `node_count` = 4). Nothing was untranslated, so no missing source and no stubs.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 40 rows over the axes the C actually branches on (all 11 entry points, global-state shapes, tree topologies, parent-slot states, label shapes, scalar boundaries, remainder classes).\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 33 rows, one per distinct rejection, with `||` operands split into separate rows, plus 5 hard-UB rows documented separately.\n- **Feature combinations:** Cargo.toml has **no `[features]`**, CMakeLists has no options, and the C has no `#if` — so the powerset is exactly `{{}}`. The script derives this mechanically rather than hard-coding it.\n\n## Phases B/C/D — 79 tests, all through both `.so`s\n\nEvery row passes across randomized inputs (fixed seed), including the low-level entry points and a hand-composed replay of `inreftree`'s pipeline. Tests run under **both** profiles and against the C rebuilt at `-O0/-O1/-O2/-O3/-Os`.\n\n## Three real problems found and fixed\n\n1. **Stale-artifact bug (critical, in my own harness).** `cargo test` does *not* rebuild a `cdylib`-only lib target — no dependency edge exists. Tests were silently verifying an old `.so`. I caught this only because mutation testing showed **all 12 mutants escaping**. The harness now rebuilds the cdylib itself and hard-fails on `STALE ARTIFACT`.\n2. **Unobservable-write blind spot.** `node->label[31] = '\\0'` writes a byte `strncpy(...,31)` never touches, so against a zeroed table a missing store was invisible. Tests now pre-poison the destination row.\n3. **Rodata fidelity in `src/lib.rs`.** `inreftree` reads `op_string[tree_sum % 4]`, which is negative (out of bounds) for negative sums. The Rust replicated a *guessed* literal pool whose comment was factually wrong about gcc's tail-merging. I replaced it with the pool gcc actually emits, verified byte-for-byte via `objdump`. Behaviour was already correct for the three reachable indices; this removes a latent hazard.\n\n## Suite adequacy\n\n`./mutation_test.sh` injects 34 known bugs: **34 caught, 0 escaped**. This is what turned a vacuously-passing suite into a meaningful one.\n\n## Documented divergences (all hard UB, all unreachable from the public API)\n\n| trigger | C | Rust |\n|---|---|---|\n| `divide_op/modulo_op(INT_MIN, -1)` | SIGFPE (measured in a child process) | `-2147483648` / `0` |\n| `node_count > 50`, then `find_node_by_id` | returns `&node_table[50]`, which **aliases `node_count`** (linker put it at `node_table+2600`) | `NULL` (`node_count` is 4 bytes *before* the table) |\n| cyclic child id | stack overflow | stack overflow — asserted **identical** termination |\n\nA hardware trap isn't reproducible from safe Rust, and the BSS ordering of two independent objects isn't something a translation can portably control — so these are recorded rather than \"fixed\". Each requires input that is already UB in C, and `inreftree` cannot reach any of them.\n\n`./run_verification.sh` reproduces everything end to end; `c_src/` was not modified (only the `build/` directory the task specifies)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1117,"cache_read_input_tokens":217029,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1117,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e1c21d0a-4bcf-4f52-9a28-e367512a5538","uuid":"04f70438-373e-46a8-9a74-f8249f9657f5","timestamp":"2026-08-19T21:34:47.717Z"}
